{
 "about": "Figures of merit over those of the current data vector when cross pairs are added along one axis (gap<=g: the current pairs + every pair whose raw n(z) ranges are at most g bin widths apart). Extracted by notes/cross_correlations/plots/make_pair_axes_data.py from the per-layout fits of scripts/compute_pair_axes_fits.py: one Fisher derivative base per layout on its largest pair list (the archived final-tier caches model_*_<layout>_pairmax_final), every point a row selection from it. Models: paper: B tilts noA2 sv x6 on the pessimistic prior (alpha_2 fixed at 0, sigma_v widths x6); reference: B tilts on the pessimistic prior (alpha_2 free, exploration sigma_v widths): the model of the pair_threshold figure. Variants: free = sigma_v fitted; fixed = the same model with every sigma_v column removed (held at the fiducial). k_max is the z = 0 value of a per-bin cut at k_max/D(zbar_i).",
